@startuml usecase
!pragma layout smetana
title COLORS Web Application - Use Case Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "User" as User
actor "MySQL Database\n(COP4331)" as DB <<system>>

rectangle "COLORS Web Application" {
  usecase "Log In" as UC_Login
  usecase "Verify Credentials" as UC_Verify
  usecase "Save Session Cookie" as UC_Save
  usecase "Open Color Page" as UC_Open
  usecase "Read Session Cookie" as UC_Read
  usecase "Search Colors" as UC_Search
  usecase "Add Color" as UC_Add
  usecase "Log Out" as UC_Logout
}

User --> UC_Login
User --> UC_Open
User --> UC_Search
User --> UC_Add
User --> UC_Logout

UC_Login ..> UC_Verify : <<include>>
UC_Save ..> UC_Login : <<extend>>\n[login succeeds]
UC_Open ..> UC_Read : <<include>>

UC_Verify --> DB
UC_Search --> DB
UC_Add --> DB

note right of UC_Read
  Runs when color.html loads.
  If no userId is in the cookie,
  the user is sent back to index.html.
end note

note right of UC_Search
  Search, Add, and Log Out are only
  reachable from color.html, after login.
  Search does partial (LIKE) matching
  on the logged-in user's colors only.
end note

note as N_Unsupported
  Not supported by the system:
  registration, editing colors,
  deleting colors.
end note
UC_Logout .. N_Unsupported
@enduml
